WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.890
Ask anyone who has ever lived in a small town
and they’ll most likely all tell you the

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:11.070
same exact thing: The worst part isn’t just
being far away from the nearest city, or distant

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.700
from friends and family.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:18.230
It’s the boredom that gets you, having so
little nearby gives you so few options for

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.330
things to fill your time with.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.170
For some, they get used to it.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:26.800
As they grow old, spending their life in the
same tiny community, they either learn to

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.860
make their own entertainment or just get used
to the boredom, drowning it out by sitting

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:34.100
and watching TV all day.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.850
But others, they just can’t stand being
bored, being stuck somewhere with nothing

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:45.140
interesting to do, and ultimately, they can
end up getting so sick of it that there’s

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.980
only one option: leave.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:54.149
Pack their bags and hit the road, up sticks
and move to a new place far from the small

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:55.859
town they were born in.

00:00:55.859 --> 00:00:59.109
Thing is, leaving isn’t cheap.

00:00:59.109 --> 00:01:04.259
Moving to a new town, a big city or even an
entirely different state is a luxury that

00:01:04.259 --> 00:01:06.500
costs a pretty penny.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:12.030
Some might work, and save their wages until
they can realize that dream of moving away.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.260
But not everyone has that much patience, some
want to be free of the boredom as soon as

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:18.370
they can.

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:23.380
Maybe they might apply to be a contestant
on a game show, chance it all and try to win

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.130
themselves a big cash prize.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:31.650
Sure, it’s a hell of a gamble, and a loss
might mean humiliation in front of everyone

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:37.679
you kow and more, but winning could be your
ticket away from small-town living.

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:40.079
That might be easier said than done though.

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:44.710
Not only does someone looking to move away
need to be picked as a contestant, they also

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.880
need to play by the rules and actually win
the game.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:53.909
But as if that wasn’t enough, they also
have to live to tell about it…

00:01:53.909 --> 00:01:58.249
For as long as she could remember, Kat had
always hated it here.

00:01:58.249 --> 00:02:04.620
Her hometown was tiny, too small to include
more than the main street with few local stores,

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:08.780
the one school that everyone who had ever
lived there had studied at, and little else

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:09.780
of note.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.320
And as for things people could do for fun
in town?

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:18.470
Well, as you can probably imagine, the options
were severely limited, especially for a group

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.680
of teenagers like Kat and her friends.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:25.940
Most of the time all that she and the others
– Leo, Ricky, and Dani – could do to pass

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:31.140
the time was sit in the back of Ricky’s
truck and park in the middle of town, watching

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:36.410
people and waiting for something even mildly
interesting to happen… not that it ever

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.410
did.

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:41.390
The four of them had a name for the rest of
the townsfolk, everyone that had lived there

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:47.610
for their entire lives and never dared to
venture anywhere else; ‘lifers’, as in

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:53.530
they were imprisoned, serving a life sentence
in this small town, never to escape or move

00:02:53.530 --> 00:02:56.190
on or make something of themselves.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:03:00.340
As much as they liked to poke fun at those
people, each of the group knew that every

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:05.470
weekend they wasted just sitting around, the
closer they were getting to one day becoming

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:06.870
lifers themselves.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:12.650
“We need to just go,” Kat would say, trying
to rally the other three into taking a spontaneous

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.830
trip away as a group.

00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:19.350
“Just load the truck up one day, pick a
direction and drive until we find somewhere.”

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:24.200
Ricky and Leo would nod their heads in agreement,
and Dani would talk for hours about all the

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:30.150
places she might like to go one day, but none
of them ever actually made any plans to leave.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:35.810
Nobody knew where to start… until they heard
rumors about an abandoned TV studio just outside

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:36.810
of town.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:41.590
Apparently, according to Dani’s older brother,
it had been there for years, just sitting

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.480
there completely empty.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:48.100
It wasn’t just a small local studio either,
one of the big national networks had owned

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.950
it and used to film there regularly back in
the day.

00:03:50.950 --> 00:03:54.180
“Why would someone set up a studio here
of all places?”

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:55.740
had been Leo’s immediate response.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:58.370
“Look at where we live,” Kat replied.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:03.090
“It’s the literal middle of nowhere, the
network must have got the land dirt cheap.

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.620
The real question is, why don’t we go and
check it out?”

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.620
“What for?”

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:07.710
Dani asked.

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:11.870
Kat silently gestured at the cramped main
street that surrounded them, the place that

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:16.150
may as well have been the center of the known
universe to the four teenage friends.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.030
“Do you see anything else to do around here?”

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.990
Before long, the four of them were in agreement.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:25.350
Ricky’s truck pulled up in front of their
houses in the middle of the night, and under

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:30.470
the cover of darkness, they drove out towards
what was left of the TV studio.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:35.780
This was it, they were finally going somewhere
beyond the choking, cramped confines of their

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.410
tiny hometown…

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:41.040
although whether or not they’d all make
it back was another matter.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:45.530
Here’s a hard lesson for you, kids: You
can’t fight for the life you believe you

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:49.870
deserve if you don’t have a little skin
in the game…

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.940
With home a few miles in the rear-view mirror,
the truck stopped at a chain-link fence.

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.980
A pair of signs were hanging from it; one
welcoming them to the studio, while the other

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.360
simultaneously warned them to keep out, that
this area was private property.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.760
Ignoring it, the four of them stepped out
of the truck and started to climb the fence,

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.250
throwing Leo’s jacket over the top to avoid
injury.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.970
Beyond the fence was a huge building, almost
the size of a warehouse, with a door marked

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:21.340
‘Studio Entrance’ that practically invited
the intrepid teens to open it up and have

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.920
a look inside.

00:05:22.920 --> 00:05:27.290
Each one of them carrying a torch in hand,
the group walked up to the abandoned studio

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:31.910
and gently pried open the door, trying not
to make too much noise.

00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:35.430
Even though they knew the whole place was
abandoned, they still didn’t want to attract

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.600
too much attention and get caught trespassing.

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:43.570
The lights were all dead as Kat led the group,
her hand being tightly squeezed by Dani next

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:45.880
to her, the two boys behind.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:49.889
None of them had been sure what to expect,
it wasn’t exactly like anyone in the group

00:05:49.889 --> 00:05:53.340
had ever set foot inside a TV studio before.

00:05:53.340 --> 00:05:58.320
But they were met with a narrow, concrete-walled
corridor, so underwhelming that it almost

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:02.180
made it extraordinary in just how profoundly
dull it was.

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:08.751
Lifting his torch, Leo pointed out some lettering
on the wall that read ‘To TMDG Set’, with

00:06:08.751 --> 00:06:12.480
an arrow pointing them four friends further
down the corridor.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:17.970
Naturally, driven by her curiosity and need
to be literally anywhere apart from her hometown,

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:21.010
Kat followed the arrow’s direction to another
door.

00:06:21.010 --> 00:06:26.950
Pushing it open, she stepped inside, her torchlight
immediately being blocked by a thick curtain.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:30.550
Brushing her hand against the material, she
started looking for a parting.

00:06:30.550 --> 00:06:32.330
But before she could…

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.540
“Welcome, contestants!”

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:40.020
a voice boomed through the dark, coming from
somewhere in the space beyond the curtain.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:44.890
Instantly, Dani screamed at the sound, almost
wrenching Kat’s arm off in sheer surprise.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.820
“Before we begin,” the voice continued.

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:51.750
“I need you all to tell me, are you ready?”

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:55.390
Kat shot a look back at Ricky, the friend
furthest behind her.

00:06:55.390 --> 00:07:00.230
Fumbling with the door they’d entered through;
it was locked, he couldn’t get it to budge.

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:03.850
He turned and met Kat’s gaze, shaking his
head.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:08.430
“Sure, we’re ready,” Leo suddenly piped
up, calling out to answer the voice.

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:12.980
Before the rest of the group could turn and
glare at him, the curtain around them lifted.

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:17.900
So much bright light came pouring in that
it practically dazed the four of them, each

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:19.260
taking a moment to readjust.

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:25.040
When her vision cleared, Kat saw they were
standing in a huge sound stage, blinding spotlights

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:29.770
pointing at her and her friends from somewhere
above, with a seating area big enough to seat

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.220
their town’s entire population.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:37.190
“In that case, folks, you know what time
it is,” came the voice again, talking as

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:41.840
if there was a live studio audience present,
despite every chair being unoccupied.

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:46.660
“These four lucky challengers will go head-to-head,
each one looking to take home the victory

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.470
as well as a huge mystery prize.

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:54.460
But only if they dare to take on The Most
Dangerous Game!”

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:59.790
There was a pause, as if this unseen announcer
was waiting for a round of applause.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:04.900
Without warning, more lights came on, illuminating
the space in front of the four very confused

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:05.900
friends.

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:10.540
Standing before them was what looked like
part of an obstacle course, a series of four

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.520
horizontal beams over an empty space.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.850
The glare of the light was so intense that,
even squinting, Kat couldn’t tell what was

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:18.850
beneath.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:23.920
It just looked like a void, nothing but total
darkness with four narrow beams bridging the

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:27.949
gap between where they stood and another platform
beyond.

00:08:27.949 --> 00:08:30.360
“Well, what are you all standing around
waiting for?”

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:33.519
the announcer declared, almost mocking the
four teens, urging them on.

00:08:33.519 --> 00:08:35.449
“Oh, the rules, of course!”

00:08:35.449 --> 00:08:39.419
There was another awkward pause, like the
voice was waiting for laughter.

00:08:39.419 --> 00:08:43.719
“It’s simple, the four of you will be
competing to make it through each of our obstacles.

00:08:43.719 --> 00:08:49.209
Make it to the end before the timer hits zero,
and you’ll be tonight’s big winner!

00:08:49.209 --> 00:08:52.980
But fall behind, or cheat, and it’s out
with you!”

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:58.019
A huge digital countdown illuminated on one
side of the sound stage, telling the group

00:08:58.019 --> 00:09:00.189
they only had ten minutes to play.

00:09:00.189 --> 00:09:05.420
Kat, Leo, Dani, and Ricky barely had a chance
to question what was going on, exchanging

00:09:05.420 --> 00:09:09.790
quick, concerned looks before the announcer
started urgently counting them down.

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:13.940
“Three, two… one!” he cheered.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:18.399
Simultaneously, the four teenagers felt a
presence looming behind them, like a figure

00:09:18.399 --> 00:09:22.860
was standing just out of view, blocking them
from turning back.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:26.399
Carefully putting one foot in front of the
other, Kat started shimmying along the beam

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:31.069
in front of her, trying to keep herself steady
while also moving as fast as she could without

00:09:31.069 --> 00:09:32.069
falling.

00:09:32.069 --> 00:09:36.689
Out of the corner of her eye, she could see
Dani on the beam next to her, doing the same

00:09:36.689 --> 00:09:39.240
but finding it a little easier to balance.

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:43.190
Leo was having no problem at all, sidestepping
with enough speed to keep him practically

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.410
neck and neck with Kat.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:46.379
But Ricky, he was wobbling.

00:09:46.379 --> 00:09:49.790
Every foot he placed on the beam, he felt
like it might give way beneath him.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:52.040
But it was just a game show, right?

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:57.180
Sure, it shouldn’t even really be running
right now, but regardless of why or how, the

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.059
worst that could happen was that he would…

00:09:59.059 --> 00:10:00.059
fall.

00:10:00.059 --> 00:10:03.619
His next step missed the beam entirely, and
Ricky could feel himself toppling.

00:10:03.619 --> 00:10:07.399
“Guys!” he called out to his friends,
trying to shift his weight onto his back leg.

00:10:07.399 --> 00:10:12.300
Kat, Dani, and Leo all froze and snapped their
heads back to look at him, just in time to

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:15.209
see Ricky wildly flailing his arms.

00:10:15.209 --> 00:10:20.269
His whole body toppled to one side, and he
dropped off the beam with a loud scream.

00:10:20.269 --> 00:10:25.160
Not one of them saw him land, or even heard
it for that matter, it was as if Ricky had

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:30.179
just been swallowed up whole by the dark void
beneath them, his scream getting more and

00:10:30.179 --> 00:10:33.339
more distant until it couldn’t be heard
anymore.

00:10:33.339 --> 00:10:34.970
“Ooh, tough break!

00:10:34.970 --> 00:10:39.410
Talk about falling at the first hurdle,”
the voice exclaimed, as if what had just happened

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.610
was some kind of joke.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.670
“So long, Ricky, we hardly knew you!”

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:47.860
Staying perfectly still, but clearly distressed,
Dani called out Ricky’s name.

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:49.360
There was no answer.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:54.040
Kat just stared, wide-eyed at the abyss below,
only looking away as she heard Leo jump the

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:56.100
last bit of his beam onto the platform.

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:00.170
“Dani, come on,” Kat whispered to her
friend, who looked back at her with tears

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.800
streaming down her face.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:05.800
The pair of them carefully stepped further
along their respective beams, trying to stop

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:10.589
themselves from looking down, or at the huge
clock, seconds ticking away and putting them

00:11:10.589 --> 00:11:12.949
under even more undue pressure.

00:11:12.949 --> 00:11:17.249
Reaching the other side, Dani dropped to her
knees, unable to hold back her sobbing.

00:11:17.249 --> 00:11:21.199
Kneeling down to comfort her, Kat looked up
at the sound stage’s bright lights for any

00:11:21.199 --> 00:11:23.490
sign of who was putting them through this.

00:11:23.490 --> 00:11:26.059
“Bring Ricky back!” she yelled.

00:11:26.059 --> 00:11:30.459
“I’m sorry,” the announcer replied,
the game show bravado dropping from their

00:11:30.459 --> 00:11:33.000
voice, “But you agreed to play.”

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.129
“He’ll be fine,” Leo said.

00:11:35.129 --> 00:11:37.589
“Bet you anything he just screamed like
that to scare us.”

00:11:37.589 --> 00:11:40.139
“Leo, you don’t seriously believe that?”

00:11:40.139 --> 00:11:43.149
Kat asked as she helped Dani stand up, wiping
her friend’s tears away.

00:11:43.149 --> 00:11:44.319
“Is he dead?”

00:11:44.319 --> 00:11:45.319
she sobbed.

00:11:45.319 --> 00:11:47.860
“I… don’t know,” Kat replied honestly.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:50.059
“Of course, he’s not,” Leo interjected.

00:11:50.059 --> 00:11:53.110
“It’s a sound stage, it’s not like this
place is dangerous.”

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:55.170
“Then why was it abandoned?”

00:11:55.170 --> 00:11:56.439
Dani asked.

00:11:56.439 --> 00:12:00.259
Leo didn’t give her an answer, either because
he was distracted by the lights coming up

00:12:00.259 --> 00:12:04.639
on the next part of the obstacle course, or
because he didn’t know and wouldn’t admit

00:12:04.639 --> 00:12:05.639
it.

00:12:05.639 --> 00:12:10.440
Ahead of them was a long stretch of the course,
forming a narrow, square-shaped walkway.

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:14.800
Wide portions of the top side were dropping
to the bottom in regular intervals, separating

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.569
the tight space before opening it up again.

00:12:17.569 --> 00:12:21.819
Every time the segments lifted up, the three
remaining contestants could see all the way

00:12:21.819 --> 00:12:26.009
to the other side of the walkway, where a
new platform waited for them.

00:12:26.009 --> 00:12:30.309
With Dani under one arm, Kat looked at the
far end of the walkway as it disappeared and

00:12:30.309 --> 00:12:33.209
reappeared behind the rising and falling segments.

00:12:33.209 --> 00:12:36.949
Then she noticed the timer, the seconds rapidly
ticking down.

00:12:36.949 --> 00:12:42.319
But Leo had noticed that too, and turned to
look at the two girls with a determined expression.

00:12:42.319 --> 00:12:45.170
Kat shook her head at him, but it was too
late.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:49.839
With all his strength, Leo shoved Dani and
Kat, both of them landing flat on their backs

00:12:49.839 --> 00:12:51.029
on the platform.

00:12:51.029 --> 00:12:55.970
He bolted towards the walkway as fast as he
could, managing to dodge between each portion,

00:12:55.970 --> 00:13:00.470
pausing as they came down, only to run into
the next one as they lifted back up.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:03.449
Helping Dani back to her feet, Kat ran after
Leo.

00:13:03.449 --> 00:13:07.420
He already had a head start, and would easily
make it to the other side of the walkway before

00:13:07.420 --> 00:13:08.420
the girls.

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:13.429
So instead, Kat held Dani close and took it
slow, methodically waiting for each segment

00:13:13.429 --> 00:13:16.850
to lift back up before they went further into
the next safe zone.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:20.949
They were gaining on Leo, who was sprinting
to the finish between the rise and fall of

00:13:20.949 --> 00:13:22.800
the ceiling’s crushing weight.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.610
Kat watched him disappear behind each block,
only to see his back when it came back up.

00:13:27.610 --> 00:13:32.480
He had made it to the platform opposite, panting
but otherwise unscathed when she next lost

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:33.480
sight of him.

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:38.410
That’s when the announcer spoke up again:
“Now, now, Leo,” it said.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.110
“That was hardly fair, was it?

00:13:41.110 --> 00:13:45.199
And we all know what happens when you break
the rules.”

00:13:45.199 --> 00:13:50.220
As the segment in front of her and Dani rose
again, Kat caught sight of Leo just ahead…

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:54.199
but it was what was standing behind him that
stopped her in her tracks.

00:13:54.199 --> 00:14:00.300
Two huge figures, each like a shadow without
anything casting it, towered over Leo.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:04.170
One of them reached forward and grabbed him,
shrouding him in a cloak of darkness… and

00:14:04.170 --> 00:14:05.579
he was gone.

00:14:05.579 --> 00:14:07.589
Just like Ricky, he vanished.

00:14:07.589 --> 00:14:11.509
Kat had been so transfixed by what she’d
just witnessed that she didn’t notice where

00:14:11.509 --> 00:14:12.670
she was standing…

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:15.119
right under a block that was about to drop.

00:14:15.119 --> 00:14:19.040
Grabbing her hand again, Dani pulled her out
of the path of the descending slab.

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:22.709
Kat felt it brush against the back of her
leg just as the pair of them made it out the

00:14:22.709 --> 00:14:26.119
other end and onto the platform, the last
two contestants.

00:14:26.119 --> 00:14:29.149
“And then there were two!”

00:14:29.149 --> 00:14:32.589
the announcer cheered, pausing again for a
reaction from the empty room.

00:14:32.589 --> 00:14:35.480
“We don’t want to play this sick game
anymore!”

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.480
Dani yelled.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:40.230
“Well, you’ve made it this far,” the
unseen host replied.

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:44.540
“Time for our third and final challenge,
the final stretch of the course.

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:47.420
Make it through this and you’re home free!

00:14:47.420 --> 00:14:53.149
But fail, or break the rules like Leo, and
you’ll be disqualified.

00:14:53.149 --> 00:14:54.149
Game over!”

00:14:54.149 --> 00:14:56.689
“It’s okay, Dani,” Kat whispered.

00:14:56.689 --> 00:14:58.610
“Whatever’s next, we’ll get through
it.”

00:14:58.610 --> 00:15:01.069
“Do you think the boys will come back if
we do?”

00:15:01.069 --> 00:15:02.230
her friend asked.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.589
Just like Leo had, Kat didn’t answer.

00:15:04.589 --> 00:15:06.600
The lights revealed the last stretch of the
course.

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:10.939
The final platform was overhead, a net climbing
wall in front of them.

00:15:10.939 --> 00:15:16.410
It was a straight, vertical ascent up, with
a wall behind the next, and holes in its surface.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:21.230
Wasting no time, both Kat and Dani started
climbing up the rungs of thick rope, staying

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.160
level with each other as they went higher.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:27.670
“And they’re off, look at them go, ladies
and gentlemen,” the announcer commentated,

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.139
still speaking as if to an audience.

00:15:29.139 --> 00:15:32.149
“But it’s not going to be so easy.”

00:15:32.149 --> 00:15:37.290
The sharp sound of metal made both girls gasp,
as long spikes shot forward from the holes

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.379
in the wall.

00:15:38.379 --> 00:15:43.420
The blades retracted, fortunately having missed
Dani and Kat… this time.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:47.679
What had started as a simple climb up had
become something akin to a twisted game of

00:15:47.679 --> 00:15:51.619
Whack-a-Mole, with each of them trying to
avoid staying in front of the holes in the

00:15:51.619 --> 00:15:53.089
wall for too long.

00:15:53.089 --> 00:15:57.489
Dodging the spikes as they went in and out,
they climbed higher and higher until…

00:15:57.489 --> 00:15:58.489
“Kat!”

00:15:58.489 --> 00:15:59.489
Dani screamed.

00:15:59.489 --> 00:16:02.620
She looked over her shoulder, only to notice
she was in the lead.

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:06.130
Below her, Dani was calling up to her with
a fear-stricken expression.

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:10.089
Her foot was caught in the rigging of the
net, kicking and thrashing wildly to try and

00:16:10.089 --> 00:16:11.089
free it.

00:16:11.089 --> 00:16:15.120
Kat looked back up; she was almost at the
platform, close enough to nearly reach it

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:16.120
with her fingertips.

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:20.739
But behind her, her friend was stuck and with
no idea when the spikes would next come shooting

00:16:20.739 --> 00:16:21.739
out of the wall…

00:16:21.739 --> 00:16:25.519
Kat threw herself over the edge of the platform
and landed on her back, just as she heard

00:16:25.519 --> 00:16:28.910
the gut-wrenching sound of the spikes extending
ring out.

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:33.540
She was beside herself, tears streaming down
her face; it wasn’t uncommon for people

00:16:33.540 --> 00:16:36.799
to be overwhelmed to the point of tears at
the end of a game show.

00:16:36.799 --> 00:16:39.550
But Kat wasn’t crying with joy.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:41.220
“We have a winner!”

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:46.100
the disembodied voice declared, barely audible
to the surviving contestant as she wept.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:49.920
After she’d finished explaining what had
happened to the police, a group of mysterious

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:54.009
agents flocked to the sound stage to lock
it down, stopping anyone else from getting

00:16:54.009 --> 00:16:55.009
close to it.

00:16:55.009 --> 00:16:59.129
They’d found a VHS tape in the mailbox at
the front office of the studio.

00:16:59.129 --> 00:17:05.380
On it was a recording of a game show, a live
audience cheering as one by one, Ricky, Leo,

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:08.000
and Dani failed to complete the course.

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:12.409
One of the SCP Foundation agents had come
to interview Kat, asking her to recount the

00:17:12.409 --> 00:17:14.370
whole story all over again.

00:17:14.370 --> 00:17:17.839
Her account lined up perfectly with everything
seen on the tape.

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:21.360
Then the agent asked her what her prize had
been after she won.

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:22.860
“A car,” Kat replied.

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:25.409
“The four of us always wanted to leave home.”

00:17:25.409 --> 00:17:31.909
Now go and check out “SCP-2030 LAUGH IS
FUN” and “SCP-1733 SEASON OPENER” for

00:17:31.909 --> 00:17:34.931
more televised tales of terror and chilling
channels of chaos to keep you glued to the

00:17:34.931 --> 00:17:34.932
screen!

